3	// Every request a transport is given, written to a directory exactly as
4	// posted, for checking what a provider was sent and cached. Tests and the
5	// shell harness only. For the n-th request (four digits, in post order):
6	//   NNNN-request.json  the body, byte for byte
7	//   NNNN-usage.txt     "<project id> <chat id>" the request was posted in,
8	//                      then each usage object the response stream carried,
9	//                      one JSON object per line
10	// tests/project_prompt/prefix_check.py compares consecutive bodies of a chat.
